BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 413.77 Tm (The first losses happen inside the registration itself, and most are self-inflicted typos. The taxpayer name has to match) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 398.55 Tm (the IRS record exactly, and Kizzy Parks had her one-time passcode verification fail because she typed a period after her) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 383.32 Tm (middle initial. She also had a date rejected for not using double digits [wNMt73DArFc @ 00:07:15]. On another) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 368.10 Tm (registration she hit the same wall by adding a period after 'Dr' [FWfV2m3K4jY @ 00:09:42]. The bigger trap is silence.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 352.87 Tm (Kizzy reports that you will typically get zero emails telling you it is time to continue entity validation, so she logs in at) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 337.65 Tm (least weekly once the process starts [eIFlVzfusWo @ 00:02:23]. After you submit, the CAGE desk checks your) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 322.42 Tm (physical address and may ask questions about your company. She warns that you must answer that email within three) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 307.20 Tm (business days and should call the number at the bottom rather than freeze [FWfV2m3K4jY @ 00:23:28]. Speed varies) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 291.97 Tm (a lot by step. Kizzy pulled a UEI in about three minutes, but the CAGE code is only issued after that address) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 276.75 Tm (verification clears. The economics are simple: a stalled CAGE code means you cannot bid as a prime. Put a weekly) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 261.52 Tm (login on the calendar, and keep the IRS letter and the lease or proof of residence on hand before you start.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 246.30 Tm (Security failures cost real money. Kizzy Parks explains that SAM.gov holds the bank account every prime payment) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 231.07 Tm (goes to. People have created dummy accounts to get in and change the banking details, and then 'poof your money is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 215.85 Tm (diverted to them.' That is why she is cautious about letting a third party register for you [wNMt73DArFc @ 00:03:30].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 200.62 Tm (Neil McDonnell flags a leak beginners create themselves: posting the EIN on a website because no one told them not) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 185.40 Tm (to. He treats the EIN like a Social Security number for the company and notes the UEI exists precisely to mask it) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 170.17 Tm ([QIEmDXcWhSE @ 00:02:33]. Maintenance is the slow failure. FedOpp says to renew every 365 days and update the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 154.95 Tm (record whenever your address, bank, or contacts change. It also says never to request a second UEI, and warns that an) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 139.72 Tm (expired registration can block awards [2Bp78kNCVGI @ 00:05:15]. When a CAGE code will not show up in a lookup,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 124.50 Tm (Federal Processing Registry lists the usual causes: an expired registration, incorrect data on file, or a submission that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 109.27 Tm (was never completed. The fix is to update the SAM.gov profile or contact DLA support [lcWf2_8nWcc @ 00:01:15].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 94.05 Tm (Treat the SAM profile like a bank login, because that is effectively what it is.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 78.82 Tm (Certification traps hit after approval as often as before. GovKidMethod warns that going over the three-year average) Tj ET
