BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 716.00 Tm (it bluntly: the prime is 100% responsible to the government, including when a sub goes bankrupt or trips Service) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm (Contract Act problems [iLuva0z2cMA @ 00:57:00]. Federal Contracts Lab frames prime and sub as responsibility) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (levels rather than status levels. The prime signs, manages, invoices and eats the performance risk, while subs plug in as) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (HVAC, janitorial, pest control, help desk or cyber specialists [3eoJWm0WffU @ 00:03:19]. Neil McDonnell attacks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (the assumption that 'prime' means 'large': a small service-disabled veteran-owned business won a $175M prime with) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm (Booz Allen and Boeing working underneath it, and an aircraft carrier runs on roughly a thousand subs [zqg5q_pZvdc) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm (@ 00:07:38]. The operating takeaway is simple: whoever signs owns the risk, and everyone else at the table is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm (negotiating for a protected slice.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm (The second point of near-total agreement: if it is not written, it does not exist. Stephanie of GovCon TechLab opens) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.97 Tm (with the classic burn, a handshake teaming deal where the sub does 80% of the work for 20% of the revenue or gets) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.75 Tm (ghosted after the partner wins, and dismisses a one-page letter of intent as a 'hope document,' because after award the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 548.52 Tm (prime holds all the leverage [JYbjE63rG-Y @ 00:04:26]. Dr. Mel lists exactly what happens without a real teaming) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 533.30 Tm (agreement: lost control of IP, exclusion from the final deal, ownership disputes and proposal hours that never pay back,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 518.07 Tm (then tells operators to stop running on 'handshakes and hope' [HKtAZzSL_GQ @ 00:01:23]. The VA OSDBU panel) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 502.85 Tm (warns that any prime offering 49% of a project but refusing to put it in writing deserves extreme caution) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 487.62 Tm ([iLuva0z2cMA @ 00:26:33]. Centurion Research Solutions sharpens the drafting standard: the work percentage should) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 472.40 Tm (name a specific percentage or number of staff, because agreements that promise 'best efforts' or 'goals' rarely pan out) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 457.17 Tm ([L-BpgTTiESM @ 00:10:18]. Across all four practitioners, the rule is identical: lock precise numbers on paper before) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 441.95 Tm (the proposal ships, never vague percentages, verbal assurances or friendly intentions.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 426.72 Tm (Practitioners also agree that subcontracting is a legitimate entry and growth lane, not a consolation prize. Humam) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 411.50 Tm (Finding Sam points out that the FAR mandates primes subcontract set percentages to small businesses, so prime) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 396.27 Tm (compliance goals create built-in demand, and a firm with zero government past performance can get its foot in the door) Tj ET
